      "excerpt": [
        "Toni Pereira"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "I build products from first principles: find the real constraint, shape the smallest useful system around it, and instrument the loop until progress becomes visible."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "AI is not the point. It is leverage — a way to search wider, test faster, and turn judgment into systems that can improve."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "x": "How I work",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "I like problems that are still partly fog. The goal is not to pretend the world is simple, but to separate what we know from what we assume; what matters from what merely looks urgent; what must be true before a product deserves more investment."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "From there, I build in loops: frame the problem, expose the constraints, create the smallest useful artifact, observe how it behaves, and tighten the system. Good product work is not a straight line from idea to launch. It is a disciplined search process."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "A few ideas show up often:"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• **Clarity before scale.** If the problem is fuzzy, scale only multiplies confusion."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• **Evidence over confidence.** Demos show possibility; evaluations create direction."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• **Human judgment stays central.** AI should expand options, generate counterexamples, draft, simulate, and stress-test — not quietly absorb accountability."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• **Trust is a product requirement.** Reliability, safety, explainability, and security belong in the design, not in a late-stage review."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "x": "What I do",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "I work across product strategy, AI systems, data, and software security — usually where the valuable thing is ambiguous, the operating model is unfinished, and the system needs to become measurable before it can become scalable."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "In practice, I help turn vague goals into testable direction; design human–AI workflows where people remain goal-setters, editors, and accountable decision-makers; and build the evals, guardrails, telemetry, and feedback loops that let teams trust what they are shipping."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "I am especially interested in the shift from AI as a feature to AI as an operating substrate: agents, eval-native product development, continuous assurance, deterministic scaffolding, and interfaces that let humans steer increasingly complex systems without losing the thread."
        },
        {
          "t": "pull",
          "x": "A demo shows that something can happen once. An eval tells you whether you can make it happen again, under pressure, for the reasons you intended."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "That difference matters. It is the distance between novelty and product, between automation and accountability, between intelligence that impresses and systems that can be trusted."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "x": "Background",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "Product leadership across AI, data, and software security; founder experience; earlier work in analytics, growth, and systems design. I have worked in large organizations and startups, often at the boundary between messy human judgment and the systems meant to support it."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "x": "Elsewhere",
          "level": 3
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• Prototypes, essays, and experiments: this site"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "x": "• Notes and work-in-progress: [@ape_toni](https://x.com/ape_toni)"
        },
        {
          "t": "pull",
          "x": "I treat intelligence as guided search: humans keep the why, the taste, and the standards; machines expand the search space and tighten the feedback loop."
        }
      ],
